abstract: >-
  Continuous Cost Governance (CCG) is a proposed vendor-neutral control specification
  for consumption-based technology expenditure, in which each material cost decision
  is treated as a governed transaction carrying evidence sufficient to support a decision,
  a named accountable owner, an authorisation proportionate to its risk and materiality,
  and an independently verified outcome against an adjusted baseline.
